===Etymology 2===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|orv|о}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*o}}, ultimately a natural expression. Compare {{ncog|grc|ὦ}}, {{ncog|la|o|ō}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}

====Interjection====
{{head|ru|interjection}}

# [[oh]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''О''' [[бог|бо́же]]!|Oh God!}}

===Etymology 3===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*o(b)}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*h₃ebʰi}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA-manual|[ə]}}
* {{ru-IPA-manual|[ɐ]}} {{qualifier|before a stressed syllable}}
* {{ru-IPA}} {{qualifier|when stressed (uncommon)}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-о.ogg|a=stressed}}

====Preposition====
{{head|ru|preposition}}

# {{+obj|ru|pre|catpos=prep}}
## [[about]], [[of]], [[on]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[читать|чита́л]] '''о''' [[он|нём]]|I’ve read about him.}}
# {{+obj|ru|acc|catpos=prep}}
## [[against]], [[upon]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[опира́ться]] '''о''' [[стена|сте́ну]]|to lean against the wall}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The {{m-self|ru|о}} form is usually unstressed except in the idiom {{m-self|ru|бок о́ бок}}.
* When governing the prepositional case, the form {{m-self|ru|о}} is used before consonants, except before a few clusters where the form {{m-self|ru|обо}} is used.
* When governing the accusative, the form {{m-self|ru|о}} is used before most consonants in the written language: the usage is variable before liquids. In the spoken language, {{m-self|ru|об}} is used in all cases.

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|ru|об||before vowels and in some other cases}}
* {{alt|ru|обо||before some words such as ''мне'' or ''все''}}

